  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 1234 AM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nA dry and warm pattern will persist across West Central Texas \nthrough much of the extended period, with above normal temperatures\nexpected. The warmest temperatures are expected Sunday and \nMonday, as short wave ridging aloft develops in advance of an \nupper level trough across the western CONUS. Highs will reach the \nlow to mid 90s across the Concho Valley and Heartland both days. \nOtherwise expect highs from the mid 80s to lower 90s. Rain \nchances (20-40%) return to the area by the middle to latter\npart of next week, as southwest flow aloft develops and a few \ndisturbances affect the region.",
